  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/acantopsis-rungthipae-2/",
      "html": "<p>All loaches of the genus Acantopsis used to be named Acantopsis dialuzona in the trade (sometimes the synonym A. choirorhynchos was also used). A recent taxonomical revision of the horseface loaches of the genus Acantopsis considers seven different species to be valid. The different species can be recognized not only by anatomical structures, but also by the colour pattern.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/acantopsis-rungthipae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Although it will stay very difficult in some cases to determine a single specimen, it is more than likely that the common species in the trade is A. rungthipae. The species A. dialuzona (= A. choiorhynchos) is still valid; it occurs in Indonesia, Malaysia, and southern Thailand, but is only rarely seen in the trade.</p><p>Young A. rungthipae from Thailand have recently been imported.</p>"
    }
  ],
